-- so the three relations are pairwise distinct, and the witnesses are not hypothetical. Each of the three
-- numbers is a count over the same six documented pairs, and each is greater than zero: the digest
-- disagrees with sameness of substance on three, the construction of the molecule disagrees with it on
-- three, and the digest and the construction disagree with each other on two. No one of the three can be
-- read off either of the others.
--
-- The direction of each disagreement is the part that costs. The digest says the same of ritonavir's two
-- forms, which are not the same substance, and of a colliding pair, which are two molecules; it says
-- different of glucose's two anomers, which are one substance in water. The molecular construction says
-- the same of ritonavir's two forms for the same reason -- it is the same molecule -- so a record carrying
-- the molecule faithfully still does not carry the substance. What the solid needs is Solid, the molecule
-- with its packing, where polymorph-not-determined is the refutation that the molecule determines it; what
-- the interconverting pair needs is Taut and Interconv, where the composition is a function of the
-- condition; and what the colliding pair needs is a digest that is injective, which collision-not-injective
-- shows the key is not.
three-relations-distinct : (a : tally-digest-ne-same record-pairs ≡ 3) × ((b : tally-defn-ne-same record-pairs ≡ 3) × (tally-digest-ne-defn record-pairs ≡ 2))
three-relations-distinct = (pairs-digest-wrong , (pairs-defn-wrong , pairs-digest-ne-defn))
